@BBuf Thanks for flagging. I checked both failed runs: it's the speed check in `test_dllm_batching_fdfo.py::test_bs_1_speed`, not a crash. On H100 the bs=1 decode speed came out at ~240 tok/s (240.16 on `h100-computable-e-gpu-3`, 239.72 on `h100-computable-e-gpu-5`) against a threshold of 250.

It's unrelated to this PR: the test runs LLaDA2.0-mini with the flashinfer backend on NVIDIA, and this PR only touches `aiter_backend.py`, which is AMD-only. The threshold was already relaxed to 200 on main in #47989, but this branch was 110 commits behind, so CI was still using 250.

I've updated the branch with main (head `2a0a5ebbf2` now includes #47989), and CI is re-running.

